   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reorganization of public administration has taken place in line with the principle of functional delineation and matching the role of government underpinned by national strategic documents</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2005-06-01" value="Policy and implementation functions are not well allocated. Staffing levels and resources do not match government strategies." year="2005">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2005-06-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2012-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Recommendations for functional allocations in line with good governance principles and government strategies are formulated andreorganization plan is endorsed"></target>
     <actual value="Reorganization of the Government in winter-spring 2010 took into account the recommendations of the earlier functional reviewssupported by the project and followed the principles of functional delineation and focus on strategic 
priorities. Law onGovernment amended and competencies delimited. Number of Central Public Administration bodies reduced from 29 to 24, number ofagencies reduced from 16 to 8.
Government strategic planning committee has been re-established and is functioning.">
      <comment>
